{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DpJVtSS6wfgFWYaoYMM3Ms","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N20_GRAPH_COMPILER result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tgraph_digest: f858289a7e2f4888a078963af151eac980c35ef931a6ee5bb079550c9262875f\n5\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N20_graph_compiler.prompt.v2.md (577a251c85b80d00fc0ae3929dc620a5c1b28b79ab970729a0b9428744f4f469)\n6\tgeneration: 9\n7\tpatch: P-N20-001 (active_patch_ids=[\"P-N20-001\"], patch_chain_sha256=ac6db487d79bdc554dbd58ecbc830e80824344e61ad9b8250711560fae5a966f)\n8\t\n9\t## Generation-9 rework — P-N20-001 (root cause: N90 finding F1, via P-N31-001)\n10\t\n11\t**Root cause chain.** N90's audit found finding F1: before any real repair/\n12\tacceptance wiring existed, a real episode could never reach `UNIT_ACCEPTED`.\n13\tN31's approved rework `P-N31-001` closes that gap by wiring D16-D23/M06 into\n14\tthe one production compiled graph (`build_curriculum_factory_graph` in\n15\t`graph.py`), additively, over and above this node's frozen 32-entry\n16\t`binding_inventory()` — which N31 correctly leaves unchanged, since other\n17\ttests (this node's own, among them) depend on that exact 32-entry contract.\n18\tThat correction necessarily makes the compiled graph's node set *wider* than\n19\t`binding_inventory()` from then on: D16-D23 were always excluded from that\n20\tfunction by design (its own docstring says so), not by oversight.\n21\t\n22\tThree assertions in this node's own `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`\n23\thardcoded the narrower, pre-correction invariant \"the compiled node set is\n24\t*exactly* `binding_inventory()`\", which is a structural consequence of\n25\tnothing downstream having wired anything yet — not a defect in this node's\n26\town topology-validation logic (`register_skeleton`, `validate_bindings`,\n27\t`_validate_topology`, `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`), none of which P-N31-001 touches.\n28\tPer this approved immutable patch overlay, the fix is a test-fixture\n29\tcorrection only, confined to the one file already in this node's write set.\n30\t**Important ordering note, confirmed empirically below:** at the time this\n31\tgeneration runs, `graph.py` in this repository still only compiles the\n32\tnarrow, pre-correction `binding_inventory()` (verified: `graph.py` and\n33\t`routing.py` hashes are byte-identical to generation 8, unchanged by this\n34\trework) — N31's D16-D23 wiring lands in a separate, isolated attempt and is\n35\trebased in afterward. The three failures the patch describes therefore do\n36\tnot reproduce in this workspace; the fix is verified as correct by\n37\tconstruction instead (below), exactly as the patch instructs.\n38\t\n39\t**What changed**, all in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`:\n40\t\n41\t| Test | Was (generation 8) | Now (generation 9, P-N20-001) |\n42\t|---|---|---|\n43\t| `test_the_available_catalogue_compiles_against_real_node_callables` | `set(drawn.nodes) - {START, END} == set(bindings)` (exact equality) | `skeleton_required <= compiled_nodes`, where `skeleton_required = set(G._skeleton_required_nodes()) \\| set(bindings)` — a subset assertion that holds whether the compiled set is today's narrow 32 or a later, legitimately wider one. The existing per-binding production-module loop is retained unchanged, re-deriving `validate_bindings`'s own guarantee for every binding this node owns. |\n44\t| `test_the_builder_registers_a_fixed_node_set_independent_of_any_manifest` | `drawn == set(G.binding_inventory())` (exact equality) | Same subset assertion (`skeleton_required <= drawn`), plus the existing unit/lesson-numbering check unchanged. |\n45\t| `test_an_unwired_undeclared_node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id` | picked `sorted(G.DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY)[0]` unconditionally as the pop-victim | now filters `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` to keys with **no compiled edge at all** (`set(G.DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY) - wired_endpoints`, computed from the real `compiled` fixture's edge set) before picking one, and asserts at least one such candidate exists. A `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` entry whose node a downstream node has since wired for real — even if the entry itself is left stale in the table — no longer produces a false victim that fails to reproduce `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED`; simulated and confirmed below (`deferred_victim_simulation_gen9.txt`). This is a strictly *stronger* fixture than the patch's literal minimum ask (\"was it wired\") — it defends against a stale-entry edge case the patch's own narrative did not need to name because it was describing D16's future removal from the table, not a leftover key. |\n46\t\n47\tNone of `register_skeleton`, `validate_bindings`, `_validate_topology`,\n48\t`DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`, `routing.py`'s guard tables, N31's `repair.py`/\n49\t`acceptance.py`, or D16-D23's registration logic were touched, per the\n50\tpatch's explicit instruction. `graph.py` and `routing.py` are byte-identical\n51\tto generation 8.\n52\t\n53\t**Verification.** Because the widening this patch anticipates has not\n54\thappened in this workspace yet, correctness is shown two ways rather than by\n55\treproducing a failure that cannot occur here:\n56\t\n57\t1. All 39 tests in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` still pass\n58\t   unmodified against today's narrow, unwidened graph\n59\t   (`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen9.txt`, **39 passed**), and\n60\t   the full N10/N11/N22/N23 verification command stays green across all four\n61\t   of its test files (`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_sibling_suites_gen9.txt`,\n62\t   **543 passed, 187 subtests passed**, covering\n63\t   `test_plan26_topology.py`/`test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py`/\n64\t   `test_plan26_model_nodes.py`/`test_plan26_state_reducers.py`).\n65\t2. Two standalone simulations construct the exact future scenario the patch\n66\t   describes — a hand-widened compiled graph with an extra node/edge beyond\n67\t   `binding_inventory()` (`widening_simulation_gen9.py`/`.txt`), and a\n68\t   `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` entry whose node has been wired for real but is left\n69\t   stale in the table (`deferred_victim_simulation_gen9.py`/`.txt`) — and\n70\t   prove, outside pytest, against the real compiled graph: (a) the new\n71\t   subset assertion holds under widening while the *old* exact-equality\n72\t   assertion this patch replaced would have failed under the identical\n73\t   widening, confirming the fix is not a no-op; and (b) the new dynamic\n74\t   victim filter still finds a real, still-undeclared victim (`M07`/`M08`)\n75\t   and skips the stale, now-wired `M06` entry, while the old naive\n76\t   `sorted(...)[0]` picker would have chosen the stale entry and silently\n77\t   failed to reproduce `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED`.\n78\t\n79\tProduction graph digest is unchanged from generation 8\n80\t(`f858289a7e2f4888a078963af151eac980c35ef931a6ee5bb079550c9262875f`): this\n81\trework touches only the test file, which the digest does not hash.\n82\t\n83\t## Generation-8 rework — out-of-scope `register_workbook_topology` call\n84\t\n85\t`build_curriculum_factory_graph` was found, on re-entry to this node, calling\n86\t`register_workbook_topology(builder)` unconditionally after `register_skeleton`,\n87\timmediately before `builder.compile(...)`. That call is not this node's and was\n88\tnever this node's: it registers N32's D24-D32 workbook engine\n89\t(`workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`, outside this node's declared write set) into\n90\tthe one production compile point, over and above the frozen 32-callable\n91\tskeleton/unit-path catalogue (spec section 8's D00-D23/M01-M06/D90/D91) this\n92\tnode's own `binding_inventory()` — and its docstring — explicitly, deliberately\n93\texclude workbook bindings from.\n94\t\n95\tThe regression was mechanical, not theoretical: run against the hash-locked\n96\tenvironment, `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` failed two of its own\n97\tfrozen assertions —\n98\t`test_the_available_catalogue_compiles_against_real_node_callables` and\n99\t`test_the_builder_registers_a_fixed_node_set_independent_of_any_manifest` —\n100\tboth on the same symptom, `set(drawn.nodes) - {START, END} != set(bindings)`,\n101\tbecause the compiled graph carried nine extra, unreachable D24-D32 nodes\n102\t(`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen8_before_fix.txt`, 37 passed / 2\n103\tfailed, captured before this fix). N20's own TEST item 1 requires \"the exact\n104\tcatalogue compiles ... with one START and only the real N22-owned D98 callable\n105\treaching END\" — a compiled graph holding nodes outside that catalogue fails\n106\tthat requirement by construction, independent of reachability.\n107\t\n108\tPer this node's own LOOP (\"fix one registration, binding, edge, guard, or\n109\ttopology test... never fabricate a stub in N20\"), the fix is a registration\n110\tfix, entirely inside this node's write set:\n111\t\n112\t| # | Change |\n113\t|---:|---|\n114\t| 1 | `build_curriculum_factory_graph` no longer calls `register_workbook_topology`; its only registration call is `register_skeleton(builder, binding_inventory())`, matching generation 7's contract exactly. |\n115\t| 2 | `register_workbook_topology`'s docstring corrected: it is not called by `build_curriculum_factory_graph` in this generation, and is exercised directly over its own builder, which is already how N32's own `test_the_compiled_graph_really_registers_the_workbook_engine` (`tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py`) calls it. |\n116\t| 3 | `binding_inventory()`'s docstring corrected to match (it previously asserted the now-removed call as the mechanism by which the unit path's registered edges stay byte-identical). |\n117\t\n118\tNo callable, edge, or guard changed — `routing.py` and\n119\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` are byte-identical to generation 7\n120\t(`6be93bf8…` and `87bd5dc6…`, confirmed by hash below). `register_workbook_topology`\n121\tand `workbook.py` itself are untouched and remain real, real-tested code; they\n122\tare simply not this node's compile point to wire, exactly as\n123\t`DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` (M07/M08 -> `N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS`) already declared.\n124\t\n125\tVerified: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` returns to **39 passed, 0\n126\tfailed** (`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_topology_gen8.txt`), and the sibling\n127\tsuites that also exercise `graph.py` — N30's `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, N32's\n128\t`test_plan26_workbook.py`, N31's `test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py`, and N23's\n129\t`test_plan26_model_nodes.py`/N22's `test_plan26_deterministic_nodes.py` — stay\n130\tgreen (597 passed,\n131\t`evidence/N20_GRAPH_COMPILER/venv_sibling_suites_gen8.txt`), so the fix is\n132\tadditive-safe and takes nothing downstream with it. The production graph digest\n133\tmoved from generation 7's `297f0b5f…` to `f858289a…`; part of that delta is this\n134\tfix (the compiled topology drops the nine unreachable workbook nodes it should\n135\tnever have carried) and part is legitimate downstream drift already on disk\n136\tsince generation 7 (the B-7 rework on N22/N23 that \"Invalidated descendants\"\n137\tbelow already named as landed), which the digest is designed to be sensitive\n138\tto.\n139\t\n140\t## Generation-7 rework — B-6 (blocking) and B-9\n141\t\n142\tGeneration 7 answers **N30_UNIT_GRAPH Findings B-6 and B-9** (fingerprints\n143\t`plan26/n30/model-dispatch-bypasses-d90` and\n144\t`plan26/n30/n20-tests-superseded-by-d90-d91-registration`, in\n145\t`results/N30_UNIT_GRAPH.result.v1.md`,\n146\ted79b4e2c68621519f7d85b33bd5c19b14f20e1dc7f0e029bd0bf9bc7a08ab35).\n147\t\n148\tB-6 is this node's defect and it was real. Spec 6.2's D90 row requires the model\n149\tattempt counter to be *committed before dispatch*, and every N23 adapter enforces\n150\tit by raising `AttemptNotReserved`. The section 8.2 table this node materialized\n151\thad no edge into D90 from any dispatcher: `FANOUT_GUARDS` translated D06/D06B/D12's\n152\tstaged packet directly into `Send(worker, member)`, and `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` sent\n153\tD07/D08/D15 to M02/M03/M05 on a plain conditional edge. Every model worker was\n154\ttherefore entered with an unreserved packet. It was masked until N30 ran a real\n155\tepisode: N23 proved D90 restages correctly by calling it directly, N22 proved its\n156\tpackets satisfy the adapters after passing them through D90 by hand, and this node\n157\tcompiled the table without ever invoking it. Only a real dispatch through a\n158\tcompiled edge shows that nothing calls D90.\n159\t\n160\tThe fix is N30's four-part recipe, applied to `routing.py`:\n161\t\n162\t| # | Change |\n163\t|---:|---|\n164\t| 1 | The three model fan-out rows of `FANOUT_GUARDS` (D06 `discovery_fanout`, D06B `interpretation_fanout`, D12 `model_visual_fanout`) name `D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT` as their dispatch destination. D10's `deterministic_visual_fanout -> D11` is unchanged: D11 is deterministic and reserves nothing. |\n165\t| 2 | `GUARD_DESTINATIONS`' `D07.sources_admitted`, `D08.domain_admitted` and `D15.review_packet_frozen` name `D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT`. |\n166\t| 3 | `_fanout_or_single` returns that single destination for a model dispatcher instead of calling `_staged_fanout` at the dispatcher. |\n167\t| 4 | `route_attempt_reservation` translates D90's *restaged* packet through `_staged_fanout`, so a one-member dispatch is a one-element `Send` list and an N-member map is an N-element one. It is now the single authority for D90's `authorized` value. |\n168\t\n169\tA fifth row was found by this node's own new regression test, not by N30: the\n170\tworkbook path had the identical defect at\n171\t`D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET.workbook_packet_frozen -> M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK`.\n172\tN30 could not have seen it — the workbook branch is not wired and N30 exercises\n173\tonly the unit path — but `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` is spec 8.2 and therefore this\n174\tnode's ownership, so the row is fixed here rather than left for N32 to inherit.\n175\tIt now names `D90_RESERVE_MODEL_ATTEMPT`, which is also the contract N32\n176\timplements against: D27 must stage an M07 packet.\n177\t\n178\t**No row of `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` names a model node any more, and every model\n179\tnode's only compiled predecessor is D90.** Both halves are asserted by the new\n180\t`test_no_compiled_edge_enters_a_model_node_except_from_d90`, which is the direct\n181\tinversion of B-6 and fails if either half regresses.\n182\t\n183\tB-9's two re-scopes were applied, and three further assertions in the same file\n184\tturned out to be superseded by the same change (all five described under\n185\t\"Re-scoped at generation 7\" below). All 39 tests in this node's file pass in the\n186\thash-locked environment, and the real episode now dispatches through D90 for real\n187\t— see \"B-6 verified on the real graph\" under Commands.\n188\t\n189\t## Generation 6 — B-4\n190\t\n191\tGeneration 6 is a narrow rework answering **N30_UNIT_GRAPH Finding B-4**\n192\t(fingerprint `plan26/n30/n20-skeleton-scoped-tests-superseded`, in\n193\t`results/N30_UNIT_GRAPH.result.v1.md`,\n194\t83c75350d23fadfafc804f4cc4d410a433ca43311eb83fa4c3acc65d3d152e87). N30 extended\n195\tthis node's `graph.py`/`routing.py` exactly as designed — additive registration\n196\tof the section 8.1 per-unit path — which made three assertions in\n197\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py` false *by design* rather than by defect:\n198\tthey described a skeleton with no unit path, no `Send` fan-out, and no cycle.\n199\tOnly the test file changed; `routing.py` is byte-identical to generation 5, and\n200\t`graph.py`'s new hash is N30's registration, not an edit by this node. The three\n201\tre-scoped tests now assert the same underlying N20 properties against the larger\n202\ttopology that is actually compiled:\n203\t\n204\t| Test | Was | Now |\n205\t|---|---|---|\n206\t| `test_an_unwired_undeclared_node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id` | popped `D13_RENDER_UNIT` out of `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY`, a node N30 has since wired for real | reads the example node off the live `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` (`sorted(...)[0]`, currently `M06_REPAIR_NAMED_UNIT_ARTIFACT`), so the fixture follows whichever nodes N31/N32 still owe |\n207\t| `test_every_cycle_in_the_compiled_graph_crosses_an_exhaustion_guard` (was `test_the_skeleton_contains_no_cycle_and_every_deferred_cycle_crosses_a_counter`) | asserted the compiled graph contains no cycle | enumerates every simple cycle of the compiled graph and requires each to cross a deterministic bound and to have a product exit; the frozen guard rows for the not-yet-wired cycles are retained |\n208\t| `test_every_registered_fanout_has_the_worker_to_barrier_shape` (was `test_the_skeleton_registers_no_send_fanout`) | asserted zero `Send` usage | asserts the worker->barrier shape of every registered fan-out against the compiled graph, and that the shape table is exactly total over `FANOUT_GUARDS` |\n209\t\n210\tThe one production `StateGraph(FactoryState, context_schema=RuntimeContext,\n211\tinput_schema=FactoryInput, output_schema=FactoryOutput).compile()` now compiles\n212\tfor real against the unmodified production schema, and all 38 of this node's\n213\ttests pass unpatched in the hash-locked environment. Generation 5 is a\n214\tre-verification, not a rebuild: `graph.py`, `routing.py`, and\n215\t`test_plan26_topology.py` are byte-identical to generation 4 (hashes below\n216\tunchanged), because the blocker was never in this node's write set. The\n217\tgeneration-4 blocker (F-01) was resolved by N11/N22 under\n218\t`contracts/erratum_checkpoint_ns_rename.v1.md`, which renames the `FactoryState`\n219\tchannel `checkpoint_ns` -> `checkpoint_namespace`.\n220\t\n221\tThe diagnostic pytest plugin used in generation 4 to size the blocker\n222\t(`diag_plugin.py`, plus its two diagnostic transcripts) has been deleted. It was\n223\tscaffolding for a BLOCKED report and no claim in this record rests on it; the\n224\tprimary evidence below is the real, unpatched compilation and test run.\n225\t\n226\t## Inputs\n227\t\n228\tPredecessor result records consumed:\n229\t\n230\t- `N10_DEPENDENCY_API`: 1788ebb199b74744233107585a22a361ccb3019e529635324a4bd5bb62611658\n231\t- `N11_STATE_REDUCERS` (generation 4): e5ec425ff016d84fb220f8e518733f8b43db8d31e2d86b22fe5371be1b7e2d0c\n232\t- `N22_DETERMINISTIC_NODES` (generation 4): b407400ea10fceff335daf9c1be61b9a7145b55f379f3f9197f719ddbe3b1d26\n233\t- `N23_MODEL_NODES`: d73373641ebfb1a1ad453f2056853ba0988d1cb0155dbec70c49e53a7bb5b44a\n234\t\n235\tN11's and N22's generation-4 Findings were read and cross-checked against this\n236\tnode's own re-verification: N11 renamed the `state.py:108` channel declaration\n237\t(and follows it through `FACTORY_STATE_FIELDS` / `FIELD_REDUCERS`, which derive\n238\tfrom `__annotations__`); N22 renamed exactly three call sites\n239\t(`nodes/inputs.py:887` update dict, `nodes/__init__.py:286` D04 `outputs`\n240\ttuple, and one test assertion). Both correctly left `persistence.py`'s\n241\t`config[\"configurable\"][\"checkpoint_ns\"]` invoke-config key and `evidence.py`'s\n242\tJSONL record key alone. Independently confirmed here by grep: the only\n243\tsurviving `checkpoint_ns` occurrences in the tree are in `persistence.py`\n244\t(lines 277, 686, 1114, 1186, 1248, 1264, 1324, 1368, 1399), all of them the\n245\tLangGraph config key or its dataclass field, none of them a `StateGraph`\n246\tchannel.\n247\t\n248\tOther frozen inputs read:\n249\t\n250\t| Path | SHA-256 |\n251\t|---|---|\n252\t| `plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/spec/langgraph_curriculum_factory.spec.v1.md` (sections 3.3, 4, 5.2, 6.2, 8.1, 8.2, 9, 10) | 44e63e6271cae25f14f0bc970c598d1c15da41b67ae3cdf811bbb2f2303536e6 |\n253\t| `plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/implementation.graph.v3.yaml` | ca4835f71750f93880a965a9879e508641b5f9360b82cb5cc8bdec8d57564f30 (was `implementation.graph.v2.yaml` at `96e1948f…` through generation 7; renamed and updated by N30, out of this node's write set) |\